{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"oidcRefresh"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"refreshToken"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:8AxiamSDK9SensitiveV","identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/Sensitive","text":"Sensitive"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","text":"String"},{"kind":"text","text":">, "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"tenantID"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","text":"String"},{"kind":"text","text":"? = nil, "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"configuration"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:8AxiamSDK17OidcConfigurationV","identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/OidcConfiguration","text":"OidcConfiguration"},{"kind":"text","text":"? = nil) "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"async"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"throws"},{"kind":"text","text":" -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:8AxiamSDK12OidcTokenSetV","identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/OidcTokenSet","text":"OidcTokenSet"}],"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["Linux"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"discussion","text":"Discussion"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"§12.4 rules 1–5 and 7 apply to any "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"id_token"},{"type":"text","text":" in the response; rule 6 (nonce) is skipped,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"because OIDC Core §12.2 does not require a nonce in a refresh-issued ID token."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Single-flight (§9, §12.1).","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" A burst of concurrent calls presenting the same refresh"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"token makes "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"one","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" wire call, and that one outcome — the token set or the one error — is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"delivered to every caller in the burst. The refresh token is single-use and rotating, so"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"“one call per caller” would present it N times, and from contract 1.65 a replayed token"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"ends the whole session on the server. The slot is vacated, identity-checked, only after"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the outcome has settled; a call that starts after that makes its own request (§9 rule 6)."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"The guard is per client instance: refreshing the same token from two clients, or two"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"processes sharing a token store, defeats it and is a defect."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"code":"invalid_grant","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" means the session is over","type":"text"}]},{"text":" (§9, contract 1.65). It surfaces as the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/AuthError","isActive":true},{"text":" it is, once; this SDK holds no token of its own to retry with and never","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"presents the spent one again. Re-authorize.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"abstract":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"POST \/oauth2\/token"},{"type":"text","text":" with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"grant_type=refresh_token"},{"type":"text","text":" (§12.1)."}],"metadata":{"externalID":"s:8AxiamSDK0A6ClientC11oidcRefresh12refreshToken8tenantID13configurationAA04OidcG3SetVAA9SensitiveVySSG_SSSgAA0K13ConfigurationVSgtYaKF","role":"symbol","symb